## 3.3. Mechanistic studies and reaction scope
A plausible mechanism for selective photocatalytic aerobic oxidation of amines over Ti-PMOF-DMA should be pursued based on additional results. Firstly, quenching experiments were implemented to determine the primary ROS (Table 2). The reaction did not proceed by replacing $0_{2}$ with ${\sf N}_{2}$ (Table 2, entry 2), certifying that $0_{2}$ is the primary source of ROS. When 1,4-benzoquinone (BQ) was added to capture $0_{2}^{\bullet-}$ , the formation of $N_{\sun}$ -benzylbenzaldimine was observably inhibited (Table 2, entry 3). In the meantime, when $\mathrm{CD}_{3}\mathrm{CN}$ was adopted as solvent to prolong the lifetime of singlet oxygen $(^{1}0_{2})$ , the conversion of benzylamine barely changed (Table 2, entry 4). Taking the above results into account, it is reasonable to confirm that $0_{2}^{\bullet-}$ is the primary ROS rather than ${}^{1}0_{2}$ . The electron transfer could be verified because the reaction was terminated when ${\sf A g N O}_{3}$ , a scavenger of electron, was added (Table 2, entry 5). Additionally, the photoinduced holes were captured by the addition of triethylamine (TEA), leading to the drop in the conversion of benzylamine (Table 2, entry 6). When 5 equivalents (equiv.) of isopropanol were added as the hydroxyl radical $(\bullet_{\mathrm{{OH})}}$ scavenger, no decrease in the conversion of benzylamine was detected which in turn excludes OH as ROS in the present system (Table 2, entry 7). Hence, it is realistic to believe that the photoinduced holes participated in the reaction but were not a source for ROS production. Agreeably, the photogenerated electrons are the only source for the production of $0_{2}^{\bullet-}$ . However, neither $0_{2}^{\bullet-}$ nor holes could complete oxidation of amines. Together, $0_{2}^{\bullet-}$ and hole $(\boldsymbol{\mathrm{h}}^{+})$ perform the oxidation of amines into imines.
EPR was used to learn more about the evolution of active species. (Fig. 6) After ultrasonically dispersing $5.0~\mathrm{mg}$ of Ti-PMOFDMA in $1~\mathrm{mL}$ of $\mathrm{CH}_{3}\mathrm{CN}$ for $10\mathrm{min}$ , a certain amount of suspension was taken into a sealed EPR tube. EPR measurements were carried out under irradiation with red light. The signal of electrons can be detected after $4~\mathrm{min}$ of red light irradiation (Fig. 6a). The signal decreased after $0_{2}$ was injected into the reaction system, indicating that electrons can be generated after light-stimulation and combine with $0_{2}$ . After irradiation, the signal of the porphyrin radical cation increased (Fig. 6b). The porphyrin radical cation was sacrificed by adding $33~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of benzylamine. As a result, the LMCT may be illustrated clearly. Furthermore, the trapping reagent 5,5- dimethyl-1-pyrroline $N\mathrm{.}$ -oxide (DMPO) was added to the reaction system to confirm the existence of $0_{2}^{\bullet-}$ (Fig. 6c). The apparent signal was detected irradiated by red light for 4 min. The signal sustained after turning off red light for $2\:\mathrm{min}$ , demonstrating that $0_{2}^{\bullet-}$ is the primary ROS.
A plausible mechanism is presented in Fig. 7. Under the irradiation of red light, the electrons $\left(\mathrm{e}^{-}\right)$ transfer from porphyrin linkers to the Ti-oxo clusters. Porphyrin radical cations (i.e., $\boldsymbol{\mathrm{h}}^{+}$ ) are produced to oxidize benzylamine to benzylamine radical cations. Then $\mathrm{e^{-}}$ reacts with $0_{2}$ in the air to generate $0_{2}^{\bullet-}$ . Next, benzaldimine and $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}$ are formed by the combination of benzylamine radical cation and $0_{2}^{\bullet-}$ . At last, benzaldimine couples with another benzylamine to afford $N$ -benzylbenzaldimine.
## 4. Conclusions
In summary, imparted by the solvent of synthesis, Ti-PMOF-DMA has displayed more accessible sites and larger pore volume than TiPMOF-DEF. Furthermore, the solvent molecules were adsorbed on Ti-oxo clusters through Ti O Ti bond. That is beneficial for electron transfer from the porphyrinic ligand to Ti-oxo clusters due to the lower electron density of DMA molecule with two methyl groups than that of DEF molecule with two ethyl groups. These advantages prompted Ti-PMOF-DMA to exhibit better activity than Ti-PMOFDEF for the selective photocatalytic aerobic oxidation of benzylamine irradiated by red LEDs. Thereafter, Ti-PMOF-DMA has been effectively applied to convert a variety of amines to the target imines by $\boldsymbol{\mathrm{h}}^{+}$ and $0_{2}^{\bullet-}$ together. This study makes available a new sight that the solvent-controlled synthesis of MOFs plays a key role in enhancing photocatalytic organic transformations.
